# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# This is a client-routed React Router app: only index.html physically exists,
# so without this rule Pages 404s any URL a visitor didn't arrive at via an
# in-app link. That breaks the customer order tracker outright — /orders/:token
# is reached from an emailed link and nothing else — plus every admin route on
# refresh.
#
# 200 (rewrite), not 301/302: the browser keeps the original URL so React
# Router can read the :accessToken param. A redirect would rewrite the address
# bar to / and lose it.
#
# Real files still win. Pages serves an existing asset before consulting this
# rule, so /assets/*, /fonts/*.woff2, /favicon.svg and /icons.svg are unaffected.
/*    /index.html   200
